note: Questions about a list: how many, any, every, no, all, none, totals, top N, most common, the one with the highest, per.
let scores be a list of 72, 45, 95, 60 and 88.
say how many scores are above 70.
say how many scores there are.
say how many of the scores are at least 60.
say how many scores is 60.
if any score is above 90:
    say "Someone did great.".
if every score is at least 40, say "Everyone passed.".
if no score is below 0, say "No negatives.".
if all scores are below 100, say "None perfect.".
say none of scores are above 95, any of scores are above 95, all of scores are above 50.
if any score in scores is 45 and not every score is 45, say "One 45.".
say the total of scores, the average of scores, the median of scores.
say the median of (a list of 3, 1 and 2).
say the top 3 scores.
say the lowest 2 scores.
say the top 10 scores.
say the top 0 scores.
let n be 2.
say the top n scores.
let words be a list of "pear", "fig", "pear", "kiwi", "fig", "pear".
say the 2 most common words.
say the 5 most common words.
say how many words start with "p", how many words don't contain "i".
say the words that end with "g".
let empty scores be an empty list of numbers.
say how many empty scores there are, the total of empty scores.
if every empty score is above 5, say "Every one of none.".
if not any empty score is above 5, say "Not any of none.".
an order has a customer (text), a region (text), an amount (a number) and some items (a list of text).
let orders be a list of (a new order with customer "Ann", region "east", amount 100 and items (a list of "tea")), (a new order with customer "Bo", region "west", amount 250 and items (a list of "tea", "cake" and "jam")), (a new order with customer "Ann", region "east", amount 40 and items (a list of "jam" and "cake")).
say the total amount of orders.
say the total amount of orders per region.
say the number of orders per region.
say the number of orders.
say the average amount of orders per customer.
say the median amount of orders per customer.
say the order with the highest amount's customer.
say the order with the lowest amount's customer, the order with the most items's customer.
say the order in orders with the fewest items's amount.
say the top 2 orders by amount.
say the lowest 1 orders by amount.
say how many orders whose amount is over 50 there are.
say how many orders whose region is "east".
say the total amount of orders whose region is "east".
say the average amount of (the orders where it's amount is below 200).
if every order's amount is above 10, say "All above 10.".
if any order's items contains "jam", say "Some jam.".
let limit be 90.
say how many orders whose amount is over limit there are.
for each region and total in the total amount of orders per region, sorted biggest first:
    say region, total.
let totals be the total amount of orders per customer.
sort totals biggest first.
say totals.
say totals sorted.
to big orders in sales and line:
    give back how many sales whose amount is above line there are.
say big orders in orders and 50.
to count passing with marks and pass:
    give back how many marks are at least pass.
say count passing with scores and 70.
let teams be a list of (a list of 3, 5), (a list of 9) and (a list of 1, 1, 1).
say how many teams contain 1, the total of (item 1 of teams).
say 7 divided by 2, rounded down.
say the total of scores divided by 3, rounded.
